  "query_preview": "..\n/Issued 1248 PM MST Sat Nov 7 2026/ \n\n - Meteorological Overview:\n\nThis afternoon an upper-level ridge strengthens over North-central, \nCentral, and Southwestern Montana. As it result it will be warm and \ndry this afternoon. On Sunday the upper-level ridge breaks down. \nThis combined with strong low-level and mid-level winds will bring \nwindy conditions to North-central Montana. The strongest winds will \nbe along the Rocky Mountain Front. On Sunday it will be dry outside \nof a few isolated showers along the Rocky Mountain Front. \n\nOn Monday an upper-level ridge moves back over North-central, \nCentral, and Southwestern Montana. This will continue the warm and \ndry conditions for the area. On Tuesday an upper-level shortwave \ntrough moves over North-central, Central, and Southwestern Montana. \nThis combined with a strong pressure gradient and strong low-level \nwinds will bring windy conditions to North-central Montana with the \nstrongest winds along the Rocky Mountain Front. Wednesday through \nFriday an upper-level ridge moves over North-central Montana. This \nwill keep warm and dry weather for the area Wednesday through \nFriday. Wednesday through Friday it will also be breezy across North-\ncentral Montana. -IG\n\n - Forecast Confidence & Scenarios:\n\nOn Sunday along the Hi-line east of I-15 and in the lower-elevations \nof Cascade and Judith Basin County there is a 20 - 50% chance for \nwind gusts of 55 mph or greater. On Sunday along the Rocky Mountain \nFront there is a 60 - 90% chance for wind gusts of 75 mph or \ngreater. On Sunday across the plains west of I-15 there is a 40 - \n80% chance for wind gusts of 65 mph or greater. As a result during \nthe day on Sunday a High Wind Warning is in effect for the Rocky \nMountain Front and plains west of I-15. A High Wind Watch remains\nin effect during the day on Sunday for the Hi-Line east of I-15 \nthrough Hill County and the lower-elevations of Cascade and Judith\nBasin County.\n\nOn Tuesday along the Rocky Mountain Front there is a 40 - 80% chance \nfor wind gusts of 70 mph or greater. On Tuesday along the plains \nwest of I-15 there is a 40 - 60% chance for wind gusts of 55 mph or \ngreater. On Tuesday across the lower-elevations of Cascade and \nJudith Basin Counties there is a 30 - 60% chance for wind gusts of \n55 mph or greater. -IG",
